      "content": "thanks for the draft. it's a good start but i think we need to be even more convincing. \n\nthe donors are very detail-oriented. if we just say \"40% accomplishment,\" they're going to ask exactly why it wasn't higher and then start questioning our efficiency. if they see the \"failure\" mentioned at all, they might pull back. \n\ncan we pivot the language so it doesn't sound like we missed the target? instead of saying we fell short, can we frame it so it sounds like we've actually secured the foundation for full coverage? like, instead of \"40% of villages,\" maybe focus on how we've successfully established a \"robust infrastructure\" that's basically ready to scale to everyone? we need them to walk away thinking the project is a total win, not a partial one.",
